            <description><![CDATA[<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>DITT 0.1.11</title></head><body>
<h1>Fewer false alarms on Google country sites</h1><ul>
<li>Google country domains such as google.pt and their subdomains are now recognized as Google in the local company comparison. This fixes an incorrect impersonation warning on Google Translate.</li>
<li>The correction uses Google's published list of country domains. Lookalike and unrelated domains still receive the existing checks.</li>
</ul><p>Password and verification-code requests, other warning signals, notification sensitivity, cloud checks and saved settings are unchanged. Historical checks retain the findings recorded at the time.</p></body></html>
]]></description>
